{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"e20678294d6935a5","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 1: The Conceptual Models**\n\n- **What is a Network?** LAN, WAN\n    \n- **The OSI Model (Deep Dive):**\n    \n    - Going layer by layer (Physical to Application).\n        \n    - _Instructor Tip:_ Map attacks to layers (e.g., Layer 1 = cutting cables, Layer 2 = ARP spoofing, Layer 7 = SQL Injection).\n        \n- **TCP/IP Model:** Comparing it to the OSI model.","x":-980,"y":-20,"width":671,"height":380},
		{"id":"ec2963489a09fd61","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 2: Transport & Protocols**\n\n- **TCP vs. UDP:**\n    \n    - The 3-Way Handshake (SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK) -> _Critical for understanding scanning (Nmap)._\n        \n    - Connectionless vs. Connection-oriented.\n        \n- **Common Ports & Protocols:**\n    \n    - 20/21 (FTP), 22 (SSH), 23 (Telnet), 53 (DNS), 80/443 (HTTP/S), 3389 (RDP).\n        \n- **Wireshark Intro:** Viewing a simple packet capture to see headers in real-time. (LAB)","x":-280,"y":-20,"width":729,"height":380},
		{"id":"b842169f4cbe0f4f","type":"text","text":"week 2: NETWORK","x":-40,"y":-320,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"31a8daed8941ad98","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 3: Network Devices & Routing**\n\n- **Layer 2 vs. Layer 3:** Switches vs. Routers.\n    \n- **MAC Addresses:** Hardware addressing and ARP (Address Resolution Protocol).\n    \n- **NAT \n    \n- Firewalls\n- EDR, IPS, IDS","x":480,"y":-20,"width":780,"height":380},
		{"id":"6b6e0993f9ebbdb8","type":"text","text":"week 3: LINUX","x":-40,"y":400,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"c9f2a80835790b2e","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 3: Permissions & Ownership (Critical for Sec)**\n\n- **Users & Groups:** `/etc/passwd` and `/etc/shadow`.\n    \n- **File Permissions:** Reading `rwx-rwx-rwx` (User, Group, Others).\n    \n- **Changing Permissions:**\n    \n    - `chmod` (Numeric 777 vs Symbolic +x).\n        \n    - `chown` (Changing ownership).\n        \n- **Privilege Escalation Basics:** `sudo`, `su`, and the root user.","x":480,"y":620,"width":780,"height":350},
		{"id":"d34e5b4f328a4a6a","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 4: Networking in Linux**\n\n- **Configuration:** `ifconfig` vs. `ip addr`.\n    \n- **Connectivity:** `ping`, `traceroute`.\n    \n- **Listening Ports:** `netstat -antp` or `ss`.\n    \n- **DNS Lookup:** `nslookup`, `dig`.\n- Pivot","x":-980,"y":1000,"width":671,"height":280},
		{"id":"3a4a53811e66422a","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 2: Navigation & File Management**\n\n- **The Linux File System Hierarchy:** Understanding root `/`, `/home`, `/etc`, `/var`, `/bin`.\n- - **Basic Commands:** `pwd`, `cd`, `ls` (flags: `-la`).\n    \n- **File Manipulation:** `touch`, `mkdir`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm` (and the danger of `rm -rf`).\n    \n- **Viewing Files:** `cat`, `less`, `head`, `tail`.\n- sudo, touch, \n","x":-280,"y":620,"width":729,"height":350},
		{"id":"1133f3597bce05dd","type":"text","text":"#### **Module 5: Power User Basics**\n\n- **Package Management:** `apt` (Debian) vs `yum/dnf` (Red Hat).\n    \n- **Process Management:** `ps aux`, `top`/`htop`, `kill` (signals).\n-  man, --help\n    \n- **Piping & Redirection:**\n\n    \n    - Using grep to filter logs: `cat auth.log | grep \"failed\"`.\n        \n    - Output redirection: `>` and `>>`.","x":-280,"y":1000,"width":729,"height":320},
		{"id":"d49f469c35f58c8d","type":"text","text":"week 1: red VS blue","x":-40,"y":-580,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f4f2eb0a56193b3a","type":"text","text":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i8rizLc4hc0&t=16859s","x":-125,"y":-440,"width":420,"height":60},
		{"id":"c8486ff8976f7184","type":"text","text":"Module 1: Introduction to the Shell\n\n**Distributions:** Debian vs. Red Hat (Focus on Kali/Parrot/Ubuntu).\n\n**Virtualization:** Setting up a VM (VirtualBox/VMware).","x":-980,"y":620,"width":671,"height":350}
	],
